LSToast 2.0 uses native Swift LSTPopViewSwift as an automatically resolved,
independent external dependency for CocoaPods, Swift Package Manager, and
Carthage. Its upstream source repository is:
https://github.com/LoSenTrad/LSTPopView

The native LSTPopViewSwift module is distributed under the MIT License.
The upstream Swift/LICENSE contains its copyright and license notice.
No upstream popup engine sources are vendored into LSToast.

LSToast 2.0 does not transitively depend on the legacy Objective-C LSTPopView
or LSTTimer pods. Version 1.0.0 used those pods for its CocoaPods integration;
its published tags and specifications retain their original behavior.
